<title>SWEDEN: Frontec, IBM in Internet deal.</title>
<headline>Frontec, IBM in Internet deal.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish information technology company Frontec and IBM said on Monday they were cooperating on a system for trading on the Internet.</p>
<p>&quot;The purpose is to offer the market the most complete and flexible solution for electronic trade on the Internet,&quot; IBM and Frontec said in a joint statement.</p>
<p>The cooperation involves IBM's Net.Commerce and Frontec's AMTrix systems.</p>
<p>The two systems should be able to handle deals from the producer to the end customer and ensure secure payments for consumer trade as well as business-to-business transactions, the two companies said.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
